  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $9$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+9 & >1 \\\\ 2x+9-9 & >1-9 \\\\ 2x+0 & >-8 \\\\ 2x & >-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & >-8 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & >\\frac{-8}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2}x}{\\cancel{2}} & >\\frac{-8}{2} \\\\ x & >-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>-4.$ The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248115/assets/c135701f345826b8ae0ba0cc8dab059834a7e7b968bc87067af45a2622d0514c.png)",
